,"title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T17:15:01-07:00","id":1486923,"title":"","content":"It's interesting to see how the video game progress of the World of Darkness has done:<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Visual Novels</b>: Coteries of New York and Shadows of New York have done well from a storytelling standpoint. They were also popular but they're still just visual novels and nothing major in the long term. Still, no embarrassment there.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Choices of One</b>: These are text based games and while they're enjoyable, they're also a niche of a niche of a niche. I think the original &quot;Night Road&quot; is relaly the most WOD of them all.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Werewolf: Earthblood</b>: A game that was generally considered extremely cheap and underdeveloped but it has the advantage of ACTUALLY HAVING BEEN MADE, which puts it above a lot of other ones.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>Bloodlines</b>: Well, we know it's not dead but it came perilously close to being dead and they are keeping a tight lid over who exactly is responsible for the game so much that we have no information whatsoever.<br /> <br /> 5. <b>Swansong</b>: Swangsong is generally considered to be better than Earthblood but still a very B- sort of game. It's better but basically like a Telltale game that disappointed people who again, wanted Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> 6. <b>Bloodhunt</b>: According to what I've read, the irony is tremendous as Bloodhunt is the only actual unqualified success story here. It's made more than enough profit to justify its continued expansion and has an active player base.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a hre